*begin threecounties

*cs OSGB:SD
*cs out OSGB:SD
;*cs out EPSG:27700   ; 15.4.21 - Becka replaced "*cs out OSGB:SD" with this on Patrick's advice: "EPSG:27700 gets the output into the coordinate reference system that's used by the Ordnance Survey and will be recognised by the QGIS import plugin". In aven "the eastings and northings should be recognisable as the SD coordinates plus extra leading digits for the fully numeric OSGB coordinate system."

*INFER exports on

; EaseGill data from RRCPC / Ray Duffy / Sam Lieberman

; not working yet
;*equate aeg1.ear.wm.001 pml1.link1.lk01.034			; links Easegill to Link/Pippikin at tag in Echo aven
;*equate aeg1.ear.GrindEasyStRoofTube.001 pml1.link1.lk12.033	; links Easegill to Link Pippikin via the Grind

;*include filename ; USE THIS FOR ANY DATA WHERE MAGNETIC DECLINATION HAS ALREADY BEEN APPLIED SO NO FURTHER CORRECTION NEEDED eg EaseGill-Pippikin data
*include EaseGill-Pippikin

;Added 22/04/12 RGB having spotted Sam had created a Barbondale file -hopefully more to come
*include Barbondale\Barbondale

;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
;This automatically applies correction for magnetic declination and grid north to all included surveys
*declination auto 67101  77807  373  ; Coordinates for Notts Pot
;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

; MMMMC data - Notts 1-4, Ireby, Lost Johns, Large, Rift etc
*include leckfell


; West Kingsdale data mainly diving data from John Cordingley and Rupert Skorupka collated by Footleg (Paul Fretwell) who has also collected some dry cave data
*include ../../WestKingsdale/survexdata/West_Kingsdale_System


;East Kingsdale - added 07/07/13 by Becka
*include ../../EastKingsdale/survexdata/EastKingsdale

; Richard forgot to check in this file!
;*include 3cgps

*end threecounties
